From fa180b72a7c78ecdc122b9543b8a0d6a469d1c2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chaoso85 <216391968+chaoso85@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:28:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: cityman: keep OCMEM disabled while the GPU
 is off

Part of the reference project used: msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon.dtsi &ocmem (vdd-gfx), drivers/soc/qcom/ocmem.c.
Before: OCMEM probed although its only user, the Adreno GPU, is disabled; the probe enables VDD_GFX, sets the
RPM OCMEMGX clock and issues a TZ restore_sec_cfg. A boot reset ~10 ms after its probe, before the MDP SMMU
probe that normally follows it.

Signed-off-by: chaoso85 <216391968+chaoso85@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon-cityman.dts    | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon-cityman.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon-cityman.dts
index 425bbd6973d..4d538ad3933 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon-cityman.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon-cityman.dts
@@ -71,6 +71,16 @@ &gpu_iommu {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
+/*
+ * OCMEM is only used by the Adreno GPU (GMEM), which is disabled. Its probe enables the
+ * VDD_GFX rail, sets the RPM OCMEMGX clock and touches the OCMEM controller plus a TZ
+ * restore_sec_cfg with the GPU domain off. On 2026-11-10 a boot reset ~10 ms after
+ * "fdd00000.sram ... returned 0", before the MDP SMMU probe that normally follows it.
+ */
+&ocmem {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 /*
  * Camera (CAMSS) and its VFE SMMU, and the Venus SMMU, stay off for now: on 2026-11-10 the
  * GPU-less FULL DT still reset at ~25.07 s, right after the VFE SMMU contexts (fda4c000/fda4d000)
-- 
2.43.0

